dth=\"640\" height=\"239\"></h3>\n<h3>RRB Ajmer NTPC UG Cut Off 2025</h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-12746 size-large\" src=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Ajmer-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-1024x353.jpg\" alt=\"RRB Ajmer NTPC Cut Off 2025\" width=\"640\" height=\"221\" srcset=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Ajmer-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-1024x353.jpg 1024w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Ajmer-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-300x103.jpg 300w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Ajmer-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-768x264.jpg 768w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Ajmer-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-150x52.jpg 150w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Ajmer-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025.jpg 1220w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\"></p>\n<h3>RRB Bhopal NTPC UG Cut Off 2025</h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-12757 size-full\" src=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Bhopal-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025.jpg\" alt=\"RRB Bhopal NTPC Cut Off 2025\" width=\"766\" height=\"303\" srcset=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Bhopal-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025.jpg 766w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Bhopal-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-300x119.jpg 300w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Bhopal-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-150x59.jpg 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 766px) 100vw, 766px\"></p>\n<h3>RRB Muzzaffarpur NTPC UG Cut Off 2025</h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-12942 size-large\" src=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Muzzaffarpur-Cut-Off-2025-NTPC-1024x394.jpg\" alt=\"RRB Muzzaffarpur Cut Off 2025 NTPC\" width=\"640\" height=\"246\" srcset=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Muzzaffarpur-Cut-Off-2025-NTPC-1024x394.jpg 1024w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Muzzaffarpur-Cut-Off-2025-NTPC-300x116.jpg 300w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Muzzaffarpur-Cut-Off-2025-NTPC-768x296.jpg 768w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Muzzaffarpur-Cut-Off-2025-NTPC-150x58.jpg 150w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Muzzaffarpur-Cut-Off-2025-NTPC.jpg 1096w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\"></p>\n<h3>RRB Secunderabad NTPC Cut Off 2025</h3>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-13000 size-large\" src=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Secunderabad-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-1024x455.jpg\" alt=\"RRB Secunderabad NTPC Cut Off 2025\" width=\"640\" height=\"284\" srcset=\"https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Secunderabad-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-1024x455.jpg 1024w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Secunderabad-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-300x133.jpg 300w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Secunderabad-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-768x341.jpg 768w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Secunderabad-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025-150x67.jpg 150w, https://testbook.com/news/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/RRB-Secunderabad-NTPC-Cut-Off-2025.jpg 1107w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 640px\"></p>\n<h2>RRB NTPC UG Score Card 2025</h2>\n<p>The RRB NTPC UG Score Card 2025 can now be accessed on the official RRB portal, where candidates can log in using their Registration Number and Date of Birth. This facility has activated from <strong>21 November 2025 onwards</strong>, allowing candidates to download their individual scorecard without delay. The scorecard shows section-wise marks, overall score, and the qualifying status for the 2nd Stage CBT, along with the question paper attempted and the correct answers marked.</p>\n<h3>Details Mentioned on the RRB NTPC Scorecard 2025</h3>\n<p>The RRB NTPC UG Scorecard 2025 contains following details or information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Candidate’s Name</li>\n<li>Roll Number &amp; Registration Number</li>\n<li>Date of Birth</li>\n<li>Category (UR/OBC/SC/ST/EWS)</li>\n<li>Railway Zone / Region applied for</li>\n<li>Exam Shift &amp; Date</li>\n<li>Section-wise Marks (GA, Maths, Reasoning)</li>\n<li>Total Marks Obtained</li>\n<li>Normalized Score</li>\n<li>Qualifying Status (Qualified / Not Qualified)</li>\n<li>Official Cut-off Marks (Category-wise)</li>\n<li>Instructions for next stage (if applicable)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>What After RRB NTPC UG Result 2025</h2>\n<p>After the declaration of the RRB NTPC Undergraduate Result 2025, candidates who meet the cut-off criteria will be shortlisted for the next stage—CBT 2. This stage tests deeper reasoning, mathematics, and general awareness skills required for UG posts. Those qualifying CBT 2 will move on to the Computer-Based Aptitude Test (for applicable posts), followed by Document Verification and a Medical Examination. Each step is crucial, and candidates must keep checking their regional RRB websites for updates on exam dates, admit cards, and further instructions.</p>\n<h2>RRB NTPC UG CBT 2 Exam Date 2025</h2>\n<p>The RRB NTPC UG CBT 2 Exam Date 2025 will be announced after the declaration of the CBT 1 results and merit list. It is expected that, the<strong> RRB NTPC CBT 2 UG Exam will be conducted in 13th December 2025</strong>. Candidates shortlisted based on the CBT 1 cut-off will be eligible to appear for the second stage exam. CBT 2 will focus on testing deeper conceptual understanding and job-specific aptitude for undergraduate posts. Aspirants are advised to keep checking their regional RRB websites for the official exam schedule, city intimation, and admit card release updates.</p>\n<p><em>We hope this guide on RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 helps you stay prepared for the exam! Download the <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.testbook.tbapp&amp;utm_source=Blog&amp;utm_medium=AppInstall&amp;utm_campaign=TBappInstall\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Testbook App</a> today to access last-minute preparation tips, high-quality study materials, mock tests, and expert <a href=\"https://testbook.com/super-pass-live-coaching\">Super Pass Live Coaching</a> for 300+ government exams.</em></p>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://testbook.com/blog/hi/rrb-ntpc-ug-result-2025-link/\">आरआरबी एनटीपीसी UG रिजल्ट 2025</a></strong></p>\n<h2>RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 FAQs</h2>\n<p><strong>Q1. Is RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 be declared?</strong><strong><br>\n</strong>Ans: Yes, The Railway Recruitment Board has released the RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 for CBT 1 exam on 21st November. Candidates can check the Testbook page for updates.</p>\n<p><strong>Q2. How can I download the RRB NTPC Undergraduate Result 2025 PDF?</strong><strong><br>\n</strong>Ans: Candidates can download the RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 PDF from the official RRB regional websites. Direct links for all 21 zones will be updated here once released.</p>\n<p><strong>Q3. What is the selection process after RRB NTPC CBT 1 UG Result 2025?</strong><strong><br>\n</strong>Ans: Candidates who qualify in the RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 will be shortlisted for CBT 2, followed by Skill Test (CBAT), Document Verification, and Medical Test.</p>\n<p><strong>Q4. Where can I check my RRB NTPC UG Score Card 2025?</strong><strong><br>\n</strong>Ans: The RRB NTPC Score Card 2025 is available along with the result PDFs on the official websites of the respective RRB regions for candidates to download.</p>\n<p><strong>Q5. How many candidates appeared for the RRB NTPC Undergraduate Exam 2025?</strong><strong><br>\n</strong>Ans: Around 63 lakh candidates appeared for the RRB NTPC CBT 1 Exam 2025 for 3,445 undergraduate-level posts across India. Only those listed in the RRB NTPC UG Result 2025 PDF will move to the next stage.</p>\n<div class=\"tb-related-links\"><div class=\"tb-related-links-title\">Related Links</div><ul><li><a href=\"https://testbook.com/news/aiims-cre-notification-2026-out/\">AIIMS CRE Notification 2026</a></li><li><a href=\"https://testbook.com/news/rrb-ntpc-cbt-1-result-2026-out/\">RRB NTPC Result 2026</a></li><li><a href=\"https://testbook.com/news/rrb-alp-cbt-1-result-2026-out/\">RRB ALP Result 2026</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"saboxplugin-wrap\" itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\" itemscope=\"\" itemprop=\"author\"><div class=\"saboxplugin-tab\"><div class=\"saboxplugin-gravatar\"></div><div class=\"saboxplugin-authorname\"><a href=\"https://testbook.com/news/author/nadeem-khan/\" class=\"vcard author\" rel=\"author\"><span class=\"fn\">Nadeem Khan</span></a></div><div class=\"saboxplugin-desc\"><div itemprop=\"description\"><p>Nadeem Khan is a writer and content professional specializing in the Education and Career space, particularly on digital platforms. He creates informative and student-friendly articles, blogs, and study resources that simplify complex topics for learners. Skilled in research-based writing, he focuses on content related to exams, notifications, current affairs, and career guidance. With a passion for clear and effective communication, Nadeem strives to produce content that helps aspirants and readers make informed decisions in their academic and professional journeys.</p>\n</div></div><div class=\"clearfix\"></div></div></div><div class=\"code-block code-block-10\" style=\"margin: 8px auto; text-align: center; display: block; clear: both;\">\n<table border=\"1\">\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"table-head-bg-color\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"><strong>Railway Exam Previous Year Question Papers</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-group-d/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB Group D Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-ntpc/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB NTPC Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-alp/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB ALP Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rpf-constable/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RPF Constable Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-section-controller/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB Section Controller Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-technician/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB Technician Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rpf-si/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RPF SI Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-technician-grade-1/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB Technician Grade 1 Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/railway-gdce/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Railway GDCE Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-ministerial-and-isolated-categories/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB MI Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/railway-tte/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Railway TTE Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/dfccil-mts/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dfccil MTS Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/rrb-staff-and-welfare-inspector/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RRB Staff And Welfare Inspector Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n<td><a href=\"https://testbook.com/railway-tc/previous-year-papers\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Railway TC Previous Year Papers</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<!-- CONTENT END 1 -->\n        </div><!-- .entry-content -->\n\n        <!-- .entry-footer -->\n    </div>\n",
